-c=\"1D465\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D465\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>"}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"<p>The cell notation indicates that the left side (Ag|Ag+) is the anode (oxidation occurs), and the right side (Cu²⁺|Cu) is the cathode (reduction occurs). In a galvanic (voltaic) cell, electrons flow from anode to cathode.</p>\n<p>The standard cell potential (E° cell) is the difference in potential between the cathode and anode. It's calculated as :</p>\n<p>E°<sub>cell</sub> = E°<sub>cathode</sub> - E°<sub>anode</sub></p>\n<p>At LHS (oxidation) :\n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.018ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"38.637ex\" height=\"2.953ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -855.3 17077.6 1305.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(722.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(1722.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-SO-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(458,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"41\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-41\"></use><use data-c=\"67\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-67\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1985.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"27F6\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-27F6\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(3901.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"41\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-41\"></use><use data-c=\"67\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-67\" tran